0. MISSION
You are building a demo mobile web app called CommunityPulse. It is a multi-hazard community resilience platform for South Africa. It connects residents, municipalities, NGOs, and community champions in one low-data system so communities can report disruptions, verify incidents, find nearby resources, and know when help is coming.

This app must look and feel like it was designed by a senior product designer at a top agency — NOT like an AI-generated template. Every screen, component, icon, and interaction must feel intentional, simple, and human.

The tagline is: Know early. Report once. Find help. Get services where they are needed most.

The product promise is: Few clicks. More help. Help is coming.

Build only what is specified below. Do not invent extra screens, extra features, extra decorations, or extra complexity. Simplicity wins.

1. NON-NEGOTIABLE RULES (READ TWICE)
These rules override any default behavior you have. If you are about to break one, stop and re-read.

Design rules:

Light mode ONLY. No dark mode toggle. No prefers-color-scheme overrides.

NO emojis anywhere — not in labels, buttons, cards, empty states, alerts, or toasts. Zero. None.

NO icon libraries. Do not import from Lucide, Heroicons, Feather, Material, Phosphor, Tabler, or any icon package. Build every icon yourself as an inline SVG component (see Section 4).

NO component libraries. Do not use shadcn/ui, Radix, MUI, Chakra, Ant, Headless UI, Tailwind UI, or any pre-built component system. Build every component from scratch with explicit Tailwind classes.

NO gradients. Flat colors only.

NO large shadows. The only shadow allowed is 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,0.04).

NO custom images or stock photos. Icons, color, typography, and layout do all the work.

NO hover-only interactions. Mobile-first: use active/pressed states.

NO placeholder text like "Lorem ipsum", "User 1", "Location A", "Test". Use realistic South African data from Section 8.

One component per concept. One Card. One Button. One StatusBadge. One Input. Use them everywhere without variation.

Typography rules:

Font: Satoshi ONLY. Load from https://api.fontshare.com/v2/css?f[]=satoshi@400,500,700,900&display=swap. Fallback chain: Satoshi, system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", sans-serif.

NEVER use: Inter, Roboto, Open Sans, Lato, Poppins, Montserrat, Nunito, DM Sans, or any Google Font.

Minimum text size anywhere: 12px. No 10px captions, no 11px labels.

Interaction rules:

Every tappable element must be ≥48px tall.

Every action must produce visible feedback (state change, navigation, toast, or status update). No dead buttons.

Bottom navigation must be visible on Home, Updates, and Help screens at all times.

All data lives in a single data.ts file. Screens read from it. Report submissions write to it. No screen has hardcoded one-off data.

